### NOT DONE — the live-on-dev legs

The work order asks for these three to be "watched red/green ON DEV", and for a run over the
staged AND published cohorts on dev. That was NOT done, and nothing here should be read as if
it were. This working tree has NO dev credentials: there is no .env.local (root or web/), no
NEON_API_KEY, and no DATABASE_URL. The instrument's only credential path is NEON_API_KEY ->
neonctl mint (there is deliberately no DATABASE_URL fallback), so the CLI cannot be run at all
from here, against dev or anything else.

What IS discharged above is the same three properties driven through the real product code with
a pg-shaped fake client, plus report distinguishability proved on the rendering function
directly. What is NOT discharged is that the instrument behaves this way against a live
Postgres: the fake answers queries by regex, so it cannot catch a malformed statement that
Postgres would reject. The cohort statements are exercised against a real server nowhere in
this branch.

TO DISCHARGE (needs dev credentials):
  NEON_API_KEY=<key> node scripts/unit-ordinal-instrument.mjs \
    --read-only --target=ep-tiny-hat --cohort=staged \
    --out=docs/evidence/work-order-v2-tranche1/dev-staged.log
  NEON_API_KEY=<key> node scripts/unit-ordinal-instrument.mjs \
    --read-only --target=ep-tiny-hat --cohort=published \
    --out=docs/evidence/work-order-v2-tranche1/dev-published.log
  diff the two: they must differ in body, not only in filename.
